      "text": "We want to find an integer $n$ such that $n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8}$.\nRecall that $n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8}$ means that $n$ has the same remainder as $-3737$ when divided by 8.\nTo find the remainder when $-3737$ is divided by 8, we can find the remainder when $3737$ is divided by 8 and then subtract that from $3737$.\nDividing $3737$ by 8 gives a quotient of $467$ and a remainder of $1$.\nSo, $-3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8}$.\nWe can add 8 to $-1$ to get a positive remainder.\nThus, $-1 + 8 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}$.\nTherefore, the integer $n$ that satisfies $n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8}$ is $\\boxed{7}$.The answer is: 7",
