      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to determine the remainder when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). This can be done by finding the remainder when \\( 3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\) and then using the result to find the remainder of \\( -3737 \\) modulo \\( 8 \\).\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when \\( 3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). We do this by performing the division:\n\n\\[ 3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ remainder } 1. \\]\n\nThis tells us that:\n\n\\[ 3737 = 8 \\times 467 + 1, \\]\n\nso the remainder when \\( 3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\) is \\( 1 \\). Therefore,\n\n\\[ 3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by \\( 8 \\). Using the property of congruences that \\( -a \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8} \\) (because \\(-1\\) has the same remainder as the remainder of \\( a \\) when divided by \\( 8 \\) plus or minus 8 or any multiple of 8), we get:\n\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nSince we want a non-negative remainder between \\( 0 \\) and \\( 7 \\), we convert \\(-1\\) to a positive equivalent by adding \\( 8 \\):\n\n\\[ -1 + 8 = 7. \\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[ -3737 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the integer \\( n \\) is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{7}. \\]",
